  "realizes": [
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:3024897a33256f888cc8bdf14471f8193608dad125b8f8ca27eae8694da69e33",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_walk_notes"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-5KCQCHVQ",
      "invariant": "INV-Z66EMHMH",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Calls _confined_stat exactly once per scanned entry and builds each row's path from the parent prefix plus the entry name, so the walk loop adds no path resolution of its own and each listed note costs one followed stat.",
      "role": "support"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:982283ac1245e4fc86e2fb53b687d371a42077dfb11192a3842764a6e629d62c",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_open_subdir"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-5NWBYG1T",
      "invariant": "INV-QR24S1VH",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Opens each subdirectory with O_RDONLY|O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW relative to its already-confined parent descriptor, re-checks an in-root directory symlink's target, and refuses only the ELOOP/ENOTDIR swap signature, so a directory replaced after observation is not followed.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:0d00b8c2e8b4018c2285876277245ab1007dcea03c3afde5fc22afd8cfc21409",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "list_notes"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-7RNSV7PG",
      "invariant": "INV-EJW15DXA",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Assembles the NotesListing wire payload {repo, master, notes, truncated} from the walk's rows and prune flag, and returns an empty notes list for a missing folder; this is the shape and ordering that must match the path-based walk byte for byte.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:d40680e3e52e1674571b0c9fe034680547f3e699eedd2038f71927be107959c5",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_confined_stat"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-7X2C4VRQ",
      "invariant": "INV-Z66EMHMH",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Decides confinement per entry: only an entry that is a symlink is resolved and checked with path_is_relative_to against the resolved root, and every other entry returns its one cached DirEntry stat. This is where the three per-entry realpath calls were removed, so resolution is paid only for symlinks.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:0d00b8c2e8b4018c2285876277245ab1007dcea03c3afde5fc22afd8cfc21409",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "list_notes"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-9YY9Y1E1",
      "invariant": "INV-ZJS1XY4R",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Creates a fresh _NotesWalk accumulator and opens and closes the root descriptor inside each call, with no cache or module-level state, so every request walks the live tree and sees new or grown notes.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:7e69a5c5252ce9324c46b19420334ae365601d3d20f23b9bf7101e468ec93765",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "read_note"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-AFAM29GC",
      "invariant": "INV-2DF3HS9Q",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Confines the requested path with confine_rel before reading, then serves the note size-capped through decode_capped and answers language binary with empty content when the bytes do not decode.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:d40680e3e52e1674571b0c9fe034680547f3e699eedd2038f71927be107959c5",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_confined_stat"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-DCXK7W7T",
      "invariant": "INV-413DC8XE",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Its OSError catch returns None for a child whose stat fails, which is what happens (EACCES) to every child of a readable but not searchable directory; those children are skipped and the listing answers 200 instead of the path-based walk's 500.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:0d00b8c2e8b4018c2285876277245ab1007dcea03c3afde5fc22afd8cfc21409",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "list_notes"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-HNH06VQK",
      "invariant": "INV-SMYSQKTJ",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Performs a full walk of the live notes tree on every call and consults no cache, so there is no directory-mtime key that could serve a stale size when a note grows in place.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:416b34dcc8d590457c1d5d955a2d30666170c76362f84c3fd718868b89a11977",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_is_dir"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-NGTT9WWJ",
      "invariant": "INV-DA7D417G",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Is the directory-first sort key: it treats ENOENT, ENOTDIR, EBADF and ELOOP from DirEntry.is_dir() as not-a-directory and re-raises every other error, reproducing Path.is_dir() so looping or file-traversing symlinks cannot fail the sort.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:892f36a83d3997a29e6cb53485f4a0c3dc2e005321e682b8c56e259785d82f88",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_notes_json"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-V1EWDR6A",
      "invariant": "INV-2DF3HS9Q",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L55"
      },
      "rationale": "Validates the {repo, master} selector (unknown repo 404 unknown-repo, multi-segment master 400 bad-request) and maps AuthorityError/ValueError to 400 bad-path and FileNotFoundError to 404 not-found for both notes routes.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "e3e6f8d4c246e066532296e69563c435200ae08b",
        "content": "sha256:514778fe85fae024f5331223bcbbc3e05579331473811c4d6195580566a51a87",
        "locator": {
